<title>UK: UK's Simon sells units to U.S. Terex.</title>
<headline>UK's Simon sells units to U.S. Terex.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering group Simon Engineering Plc said on Monday it sold the industrial businesses of its Access Division to U.S. diversified engineering group Terex Corp for $90 million.</p>
<p>Simon said it would use the proceeds to repay a significant amount of debt and help it restructure its banking arrangements.</p>
<p>Maurice Dixson, Simon's chief executive, said the company would repay in full its U.S. loan notes.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
